,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,37175,279,4771,315,26107,59,37018,45340,61,18,6558,61,17,37892,15170,21,87,61,17,12,24,87,92,76466,10061,400,64,3,387,279,1372,315,19766,304,279,4771,11,400,65,3,387,279,1372,315,12140,438,88,1307,6295,11,400,66,3,387,279,1372,315,16202,96254,6295,11,323,400,67,3,387,279,1372,315,1508,36426,96254,6295,13,7379,400,64,10,17,65,10,18,66,10,19,67,3,382,37314,9960,510,27,37420,91339,397,1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,23643,279,729,1124,11520,37018,45340,61,18,481,856,61,17,488,856,15170,21,87,61,17,481,220,24,87,11035,8,3019,553,3019,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,61242,1437,279,5712,198,5338,11,8168,279,63533,323,279,46912,382,785,63533,374,510,78045,856,61,18,481,856,61,17,488,856,284,856,2075,61,17,481,856,488,220,16,8,1124,2533,785,46912,374,510,78045,220,21,87,61,17,481,220,24,87,284,220,18,87,7,17,87,481,220,18,8,1124,2533,4416,11,279,729,9044,510,78045,1124,37018,45340,2075,61,17,481,856,488,220,16,9139,90,18,87,7,17,87,481,220,18,9139,1124,2533,1654,646,9121,279,4185,8168,17767,87,57758,320,65363,17767,87,1124,811,80,220,15,59,9957,78045,1124,37018,45340,61,17,481,856,488,220,16,15170,18,7,17,87,481,220,18,9139,1124,2533,14374,14822,220,17,25,64547,472,7151,198,32,14178,304,279,4771,13666,1380,2176,279,63533,323,279,46912,614,264,4185,8168,429,646,387,33446,13,758,419,1142,11,1052,525,902,4185,9363,1948,279,63533,17767,87,61,17,481,856,488,220,16,57758,323,279,46912,17767,18,7,17,87,481,220,18,10699,568,15277,11,1052,525,902,19766,382,44500,11,17767,64,284,220,15,59,3593,14374,14822,220,18,25,64547,35463,1634,1600,417,6295,198,18612,96254,6295,12170,1380,279,46912,374,7168,323,279,63533,374,2477,36929,13,2573,279,46912,6144,311,7168,323,11625,369,17767,87,59,982,78045,220,18,7,17,87,481,220,18,8,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,220,17,87,481,220,18,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,856,284,1124,37018,90,18,15170,17,92,1124,2533,4416,11,1052,374,825,12140,96254,1272,518,17767,87,284,1124,37018,90,18,15170,17,11035,3593,44500,11,17767,65,284,220,16,59,3593,14374,14822,220,19,25,64547,39909,1634,1600,417,6295,198,1249,1477,16202,96254,6295,11,582,9429,279,12348,315,279,63533,323,279,46912,382,785,8381,315,279,63533,17767,87,61,17,481,856,488,220,16,57758,374,220,17,624,785,8381,315,279,46912,17767,21,87,481,220,24,57758,374,220,16,4192,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nConsider the graph of $$\\frac{x^3-x^2+x}{6x^2-9x}.$$Let $a$ be the number of holes in the graph, $b$ be the number of vertical asympotes, $c$ be the number of horizontal asymptotes, and $d$ be the number of oblique asymptotes. Find $a+2b+3c+4d$.\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\(\\frac{x^3 - x^2 + x}{6x^2 - 9x}\\) step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the Function\nFirst, factor the numerator and the denominator.\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[ x^3 - x^2 + x = x(x^2 - x + 1) \\]\n\nThe denominator is:\n\\[ 6x^2 - 9x = 3x(2x - 3) \\]\n\nSo, the function becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{x(x^2 - x + 1)}{3x(2x - 3)} \\]\n\nWe can cancel the common factor \\(x\\) (assuming \\(x \\neq 0\\)):\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{3(2x - 3)} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify Holes\nA hole in the graph occurs where both the numerator and the denominator have a common factor that can be canceled. In this case, there are no common factors between the numerator \\(x^2 - x + 1\\) and the denominator \\(3(2x - 3)\\). Therefore, there are no holes.\n\nThus, \\(a = 0\\).\n\n### Step 3: Identify Vertical Asymptotes\nVertical asymptotes occur where the denominator is zero and the numerator is non-zero. Set the denominator equal to zero and solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[ 3(2x - 3) = 0 \\]\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\nSo, there is one vertical asymptote at \\(x = \\frac{3}{2}\\).\n\nThus, \\(b = 1\\).\n\n### Step 4: Identify Horizontal Asymptotes\nTo find horizontal asymptotes, we compare the degrees of the numerator and the denominator.\n\nThe degree of the numerator \\(x^2 - x + 1\\) is 2.\nThe degree of the denominator \\(6x - 9\\) is 1.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7e89cf8b20e17c9b8544628105ac192121ae86fec720f7767444be1f36d57166"},"seconds":47.91200494766235,"seed":56619237533513647,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\(\\frac{x^3 - x^2 + x}{6x^2 - 9x}\\) step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the Function\nFirst, factor the numerator and the denominator.\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[ x^3 - x^2 + x = x(x^2 - x + 1) \\]\n\nThe denominator is:\n\\[ 6x^2 - 9x = 3x(2x - 3) \\]\n\nSo, the function becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{x(x^2 - x + 1)}{3x(2x - 3)} \\]\n\nWe can cancel the common factor \\(x\\) (assuming \\(x \\neq 0\\)):\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{3(2x - 3)} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify Holes\nA hole in the graph occurs where both the numerator and the denominator have a common factor that can be canceled. In this case, there are no common factors between the numerator \\(x^2 - x + 1\\) and the denominator \\(3(2x - 3)\\) other than \\(x\\). Since we already canceled \\(x\\), there are no holes in the graph.\n\nThus, \\(a = 0\\).\n\n### Step 3: Identify Vertical Asymptotes\nVertical asymptotes occur where the denominator is zero and the numerator is non-zero. Set the denominator equal to zero and solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[ 3(2x - 3) = 0 \\]\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\nSo, there is one vertical asymptote at \\(x = \\frac{3}{2}\\).\n\nThus, \\(b = 1\\).\n\n### Step 4: Identify Horizontal Asymptotes\nTo determine horizontal asymptotes, we compare the degrees of the numerator and the denominator. After simplification, the function is:\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{3(2x - 3)} = \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{6x - 9} \\]\n\nThe degree of the numerator is 2, and the degree of the denominator is 1. Since the degree of the numerator is greater than the degree of the denominator, there is no horizontal asymptote.\n\nThus, \\(c = 0\\).\n\n### Step 5: Identify Oblique Asymptotes\nSince the degree of the numerator is greater than the degree of the denominator by 1, there is an oblique asymptote. To find it, we perform polynomial long division of the numerator by the denominator. However, without explicitly performing the division, we can determine that there is exactly one oblique asymptote.\n\nThus, \\(d = 1\\).\n\n### Step 6: Calculate \\(a + 2b + 3c + 4d\\)\nNow, we substitute the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) into the expression \\(a + 2b + 3c + 4d\\):\n\\[ a + 2b + 3c + 4d = 0 + 2(1) + 3(0) + 4(1) = 0 + 2 + 0 + 4 = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\(\\frac{x^3 - x^2 + x}{6x^2 - 9x}\\) step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the Function\nFirst, factor the numerator and the denominator.\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[ x^3 - x^2 + x = x(x^2 - x + 1) \\]\n\nThe denominator is:\n\\[ 6x^2 - 9x = 3x(2x - 3) \\]\n\nSo, the function becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{x(x^2 - x + 1)}{3x(2x - 3)} \\]\n\nWe can cancel the common factor \\(x\\) (assuming \\(x \\neq 0\\)):\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{3(2x - 3)} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify Holes\nA hole in the graph occurs where both the numerator and the denominator have a common factor that can be canceled. In this case, there are no common factors between the numerator \\(x^2 - x + 1\\) and the denominator \\(3(2x - 3)\\) other than \\(x\\). Since we already canceled \\(x\\), there are no holes in the graph.\n\nThus, \\(a = 0\\).\n\n### Step 3: Identify Vertical Asymptotes\nVertical asymptotes occur where the denominator is zero and the numerator is non-zero. Set the denominator equal to zero and solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[ 3(2x - 3) = 0 \\]\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\nSo, there is one vertical asymptote at \\(x = \\frac{3}{2}\\).\n\nThus, \\(b = 1\\).\n\n### Step 4: Identify Horizontal Asymptotes\nTo determine horizontal asymptotes, we compare the degrees of the numerator and the denominator. After simplification, the function is:\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{3(2x - 3)} = \\frac{x^2 - x + 1}{6x - 9} \\]\n\nThe degree of the numerator is 2, and the degree of the denominator is 1. Since the degree of the numerator is greater than the degree of the denominator, there is no horizontal asymptote.\n\nThus, \\(c = 0\\).\n\n### Step 5: Identify Oblique Asymptotes\nSince the degree of the numerator is greater than the degree of the denominator by 1, there is an oblique asymptote. To find it, we perform polynomial long division of the numerator by the denominator. However, without explicitly performing the division, we can determine that there is exactly one oblique asymptote.\n\nThus, \\(d = 1\\).\n\n### Step 6: Calculate \\(a + 2b + 3c + 4d\\)\nNow, we substitute the values of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) into the expression \\(a + 2b + 3c + 4d\\):\n\\[ a + 2b + 3c + 4d = 0 + 2(1) + 3(0) + 4(1) = 0 + 2 + 0 + 4 = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]","id":"intermediate_algebra:881"}
